From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim <tim@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: nuvoton: npcm845-evb: enable JTAG Master 2

Enable jtm2. Its pinctrl (jm2_pins) sets MFSEL5.JM2SEL so the JS_* pins
on J_JTAGS_A35 are driven by JTAG Master 2 instead of the JTAG2 slave.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [EVB test]
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nuvoton/nuvoton-npcm845-evb.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nuvoton/nuvoton-npcm845-evb.dts
index c567b09..f20fc6f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nuvoton/nuvoton-npcm845-evb.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nuvoton/nuvoton-npcm845-evb.dts
@@ -436,6 +436,15 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/*
+ * JTAG Master 2: pinctrl jm2_pins sets MFSEL5.JM2SEL (bit 1), which moves
+ * the JS_TCK/TMS/TDI/TDO/nTRST pins (J_JTAGS_A35 header) from the
+ * JTAG2 slave to JTAG Master 2. JTAG2 slave is unavailable while enabled.
+ */
+&jtm2 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &rng {
 	status = "okay";
 };
